Xbox loader hello example
=========================

This is a freestanding loader diagnostic. It prints "Hello, Xbox!" through
kos-tool's xbox-load-ip service without linking against KOS. It is retained so
the loader ABI can be tested independently of the KOS Xbox runtime.

xbox-load-ip places its guest header at XBOX_KOSLOAD_BASE (0x00011000). The
header contains the 0xdeadbeef magic value and a syscall entry point. start()
checks the magic value, writes the message, and invokes the loader exit call.

Build it with the toolchain selected by environ.sh:

    make

An explicit compiler prefix may also be supplied:

    make XBOX_TARGET=/opt/toolchains/xbox/i686-pc-xbox/bin/i686-pc-xbox

The PE/COFF hello.exe retains symbols for debugging. hello.elf is the stripped
elf32-i386 image consumed by xbox-load-ip.

Run xbox-load-ip on the console, then execute:

    make run

KOS-linked Xbox examples use the architecture startup code, Xbox linker
script, shared KOSLoad driver, libc, and threading runtime. This example uses
the raw loader interface and therefore helps distinguish loader problems from
KOS runtime problems. Neither path provides a local video console yet.
